The issue persists: extra quote after JSON. Need to ensure no stray quote. The <action_input> expects a JSON object. So we need:

<action_input>{"route":"{\"type\": \"mol\", \"smiles\": \"COc1ccc(C(=CH2)c2ccc(OC)cc2)cc1\", \"children\": [{\"type\": \"reaction\", \"template_id\": 1679747, \"children\": [{\"type\": \"mol\", \"smiles\": \"COc1ccc(C(=O)c2ccc(OC)cc2)cc1\"}, {\"type\": \"mol\", \"smiles\": \"[Li]C[Si](C)(C)C\"}]}]}"}"</action_input>

But still extra quote after outer }. Actually the outer JSON ends with } then the string ends with " then outer JSON ends with }. So we need:

{"route":"{...}"} . So after the escaped inner JSON, we have a closing double quote, then close outer brace. No extra quote after that. So the correct text is:

<action_input>{"route":"{\"type\": \"mol\", \"smiles\": \"COc1ccc(C(=CH2)c2ccc(OC)cc2)cc1\", \"children\": [{\"type\": \"reaction\", \"template_id\": 1679747, \"children\": [{\"type\": \"mol\", \"smiles\": \"COc1ccc(C(=O)c2ccc(OC)cc2)cc1\"}, {\"type\": \"mol\", \"smiles\": \"[Li]C[Si](C)(C)C\"}]}]}"}"</action_input>

Wait there is still a trailing quote after the outer }. Actually we have ..."}"} . That's two quotes before closing brace. The correct is ..."}"}? Let's write step by step:

outer JSON: { "route": "INNER" }

So string: {"route":"INNER"}

INNER is escaped JSON: "{\"type\": \"mol\", ... }"

Thus final: {"route":"{\"type\": \"mol\", ... }"}

So after the escaped inner JSON, we have a closing double quote for the value, then close outer brace. So the characters: ... }"}   (inner ends with } then escaped as \}, then the outer string ends with " then } . So the final characters are }"} . That's correct: }"} . No extra quote after outer }. So the earlier version had an extra quote after outer } (i.e., }"}"). That would be }"}". So we need only one quote before the final }. So the correct is ... }"} }? Wait we need to close outer brace after the quote. So ... }"} }? Actually we need: ... }"} }? Let's write full:

{"route":"{\"type\": \"mol\", \"smiles\": \"...\", \"children\": [{...}]}"} 

Yes that's it. So after the escaped inner JSON, we have a closing double quote, then a closing brace. So the string ends with }"} . That's correct.

Thus our action_input should be:

{"route":"{\"type\": \"mol\", \"smiles\": \"COc1ccc(C(=CH2)c2ccc(OC)cc2)cc1\", \"children\": [{\"type\": \"reaction\", \"template_id\": 1679747, \"children\": [{\"type\": \"mol\", \"smiles\": \"COc1ccc(C(=O)c2ccc(OC)cc2)cc1\"}, {\"type\": \"mol\", \"smiles\": \"[Li]C[Si](C)(C)C\"}]}]}"}

Now ensure no extra quotes. Let's produce that.
